    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0373" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg313"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>If the proposed release is accepted, it leaves Waller the same rights and
                    remedies before French tribunals as would under like circumstances be available
                    to a foreigner.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d346-f1"/> The foreign office will then
                    require an exchange of letters with this embassy that the incident is closed
                    between the two Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d346-f1" n="1" xml:id="d346-f1-content">
                <p>Frenchman.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
